<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN"
  "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!-- EyeGuard Find My cross-check (2026-08-31) -- see
     eyeguard/findmy_watcher.py's module docstring for the full reasoning.
     Installed to /Library/LaunchAgents (root-owned, so the monitored user
     runs it but can't edit it -- same pattern as com.eyeguard.monitor.plist),
     runs as the monitored user (no root needed -- only reads a credential
     file in the user's own data directory). LimitLoadToSessionType Aqua,
     matching com.eyeguard.monitor.plist's proven-working setting.

     LABEL RENAMED from com.eyeguard.findmy to com.eyeguard.findmywatcher
     (2026-09-01), confirmed necessary via direct isolation testing: the
     original label failed 'Bootstrap failed: 5: Input/output error' on
     EVERY attempt (bootstrap, bootout, load, across multiple session-type
     variants, across a full reboot) -- but a throwaway plist with identical
     content and a FRESH label bootstrapped cleanly on the first try, and
     the original label failed again even stripped down to nothing but
     Label+ProgramArguments+RunAtLoad. `sfltool dumpbtm` showed multiple
     different "generations" already registered for the original identifier
     from the earlier failed attempts -- launchd/Background Task Management
     appears to have gotten this specific label into a stuck/corrupted
     registration state that neither bootstrap nor bootout could clear.
     Renaming sidesteps it entirely rather than chasing the corrupted state
     further. If this ever recurs for some OTHER label in this project,
     renaming (not endless bootstrap/bootout retries) is the fix that
     actually worked here.

     StandardOutPath/StandardErrorPath point at the user-writable data dir,
     NOT the root-owned code tree -- learned from the pending_uploads.jsonl
     PermissionError incident (2026-08-27) earlier in this same project. -->
<plist version="1.0"><dict>
  <key>Label</key><string>com.eyeguard.findmywatcher</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/Applications/EyeGuard.app/Contents/Resources/python/bin/python3.12</string>
    <string>-m</string>
    <string>eyeguard.findmy_watcher</string>
    <string>--config</string>
    <string>/Library/Application Support/EyeGuard/config.yaml</string>
  </array>
  <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
  <string>/Library/Application Support/EyeGuard</string>
  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>PYTHONPATH</key><string>/Library/Application Support/EyeGuard</string>
  </dict>
  <key>LimitLoadToSessionType</key><string>Aqua</string>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key><true/>
  <key>KeepAlive</key><true/>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key><string>/Users/jonahdirrim/Library/Application Support/EyeGuard-data/findmy_watcher.out.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key><string>/Users/jonahdirrim/Library/Application Support/EyeGuard-data/findmy_watcher.err.log</string>
</dict></plist>
